description: Prefer explicit APIs over implicit wiring (context, globals, magic)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Explicit APIs

Prefer explicit props, parameters, and callbacks over implicit wiring.

- Make component dependencies visible in their APIs.
- Pass local dependencies explicitly via props.
- Pass actions explicitly via callbacks.
- Avoid global variables and hidden singleton dependencies.
- Avoid React Context for dependencies that are local to a component subtree.
- Use React Context only for genuinely cross-cutting concerns (theme, locale, auth).
- Do not use hooks to implicitly discover dependencies when passing them explicitly is clearer.
- Prefer typed props over implicit lookups.

```tsx
// BAD — hidden dependency
function UserActions() {
  const { user, deleteUser } = useUserContext()
}

// GOOD — explicit dependencies
type UserActionsProps = {
  user: User
  onDelete: () => void
}

function UserActions({ user, onDelete }: UserActionsProps) {
  // ...
}
```
